# Security & release

## Secrets
- Never commit `.env`, service account keys, API tokens, `eas-secrets*.env` with real values
- Use EAS env / server env; rotate if leaked
- Don’t print secrets in logs or chat

## App / web security baseline
- Auth tokens in secure storage; short-lived access + refresh where applicable
- HTTPS only for APIs
- Sanitize deep links / WebView URLs
- Least privilege for CRM/payment calls

## CI / delivery
- Prefer `tsc --noEmit` (app) before OTA/build
- Preview OTA (`channel preview`) for UI experiments
- Production / TestFlight / Play only when user asks
- After store binary: wait for Apple/Google processing; don’t spam rebuilds

## Incident flow
1. Sentry MCP / dashboard for stack + release
2. Reproduce on device or web
3. Fix + preview verify + then production channel if needed
